# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.block() called inside a tagged scope; block propagates from
#         the scope tag to the outer join ('&'); no deadlock.
# blocked: a chunk-top `,` group cannot share a declaration with its
#          arms, so the tag cannot be both created and named by a sibling
#          strand in one program.  tag.block() itself works (probed) and
#          the gate semantics are covered in C by
#          tests/rt/test_sched.c::block_and_freeze_are_independent.
#
# Everything below this line predates the re-foundation: it names
# tasks and entry points that no longer exist, and its account of
# what stands in the way has been superseded by the `blocked:` line
# above, which was probed against this branch.  Kept for the
# original urbiscript it carries.
# matrix-row: tag-block
#
# Reason:
#   The fixture calls a.block on a tag — tag.block() is an object method that
#   requires M4 prototype-OOP dispatch.  At M3 we have the UTag data structure
#   and urbi_tag_stop (C API) but no urbiscript method dispatch infrastructure.
#   Also uses '&' separator (M5 chk driver).
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with tag method dispatch):
# # a: { 1 & a.block };
